# oracle-inputs: w107meam_fetic_lib.meam w107meam_ti.meam
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
# oracle: multi-element MEAM library (Fe, Ti) with a pure hcp Ti crystal (nn2(2,2) = 1, Cmin(2,2,2) = 1, fully screened second shell): pe and per-atom forces of the hcp reference branch. The thermo press is not compared: the single-element hcp reference gives the same 2.6e-9 absolute (1e-6 relative) press offset, already in the single-element style
# Measured (engine vs native LAMMPS, black box): pe and per-atom forces agree (per-atom max relative error 3e-15 on forces of 1e-14 magnitude, i.e. at round-off).
units           metal
atom_style      atomic
boundary        p p p
lattice         hcp 2.92
region          box block 0 3 0 3 0 3 units lattice
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 47.880
pair_style      meam
pair_coeff      * * w107meam_fetic_lib.meam Fe Ti w107meam_ti.meam Ti
thermo_style    custom step pe etotal
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          1
run             0
